        inShort: ["**India's only maker of borosilicate (heat-proof) kitchen glassware**, which also holds about a third of the opalware tableware market through Larah and sells Hydra steel bottles, small appliances and cookware.", "**Good:** its own bottle plant started on 30 June, solar power should save about ₹28cr in FY27, and the government's trade-remedies body has recommended a five-year anti-dumping duty on Chinese borosilicate glass. **Bad:** return on capital near 11% for four years, free cash negative for four years, 282 days of stock, and net debt doubled to ₹99cr in one quarter.", "**Verdict: pass.** A strong brand with a poor record on returns. The price needs about {need:Borosil|23}% a year against my ~15%, which is {label:Borosil|stretched}."],
